WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.704
-Welcome back. I'm talking
to Jessica Biel once again!

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.040
We are joined right now
by one of the stars

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.574
of her show, "Cruel Summer."

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:11.377
Please welcome
Chiara Aurelia!

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:14.914
Chiara, hey! Wow.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.282
Chiara, it is great to meet you.

00:00:17.282 --> 00:00:18.851
Thank you for doing this.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.186
-Thank you so much
for having me.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.021
It's great to meet you, too.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.223
-There's been so much buzz
about this show.

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:28.794
It was Freeform's
most watched series debut ever,

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:30.729
by the way.
Congrats on that to both of you.

00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:31.964
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:35.034
-So cool.
-It's fantastic.

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:37.336
I was wondering
if either one of you, do you

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:41.173
ever look at memes and theories
that people have on the Internet

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:44.109
about who might have done what?

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:46.746
Or do you try to stay away
from all that stuff?

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.915
-I mean, me personally,

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.317
I actually kind of
don't look at anything.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.752
I don't know
if I should do that.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.953
I feel like people are like, "Do
you know what happened today?"

00:00:54.953 --> 00:00:58.324
And I have literally no idea.
I kind of stay out of it.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:01.194
But I have two friends who are
so obsessed with the show.

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.595
So I kind of get all my news,
all my media,

00:01:03.595 --> 00:01:05.531
all my updates from them.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.233
But they kind of tell me
what I want to hear.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.335
So, who knows?

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.905
-it really is like
so many twists and turns,

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.205
as I was just talking
to Jess about.

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:16.342
It's very mysterious,
true crime.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.811
But I heard as you were
filming it, the crew

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:21.214
and everyone didn't really know
who did what

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.216
until the last two episodes.
Is that true?

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.750
-Honestly, to tell you
the truth,

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.253
when the producers
and our creator Tia,

00:01:28.253 --> 00:01:30.056
we all decided, okay,

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:32.592
let's let this be
sort of a surprise

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.895
for everyone as we go through
these episodes and shoot them.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:39.298
From an actor's standpoint,
this is crazy.

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:42.902
I would literally not allow this
to happen.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.636
if you were not going
to tell me the --

00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:47.373
If I was in the show
and you're not going to tell me

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.075
what I'm working towards and --

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.876
How do I place my performance?

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:53.313
And I said this to these
girls and they're like,

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.848
"I actually prefer this.
I don't want to know."

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.383
-No, no, no.
-"I want to be focused."

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.686
-This is how young artists

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.321
are so much different
now these days.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:03.689
-Young artists.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:07.426
Chiara, you are --
The show is set in the '90s,

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:12.564
and you were born in 2020.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.564 --> 00:02:15.701
-Yeah, just yesterday.
-Yeah. Congrats, I'm so happy.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:19.605
But seriously, when you see
things from the '90s,

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:20.707
does it freak you out?

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.609
Do you go like,
"What are these things?"

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.777
-There was a couple
of moments like that.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.614
I mean, the biggest story
that we have is that Olivia

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.315
did not know what a Walkman was.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:33.586
So she was on set, kind of
staring at it with confusion,

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:36.656
and she was trying to, like, fit
it into her little fanny pack

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.458
and she couldn't figure it out.
It was very overwhelming.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:41.827
I had more VHS tapes.
I used a Walkman.

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:47.467
It was kind of all the '90s
gadgets and stuff.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.034
-The good old days, right,
Jimmy?

00:02:49.034 --> 00:02:51.504
-Yeah. Oh, my goodness.
Are you kidding me? Yeah.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:55.741
But I mean, Jessica,
you were on a teen drama.

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:58.144
Is it different
watching this now,

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:02.080
doing this teen drama
than it was when you were there?

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.449
-This is so different.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:09.355
And I feel like television
has changed so much for,

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:13.192
you know, teen dramas
and Y.A. stories.

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:14.894
It's so much more complex.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.730
The characters
are so much more developed,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.332
in my opinion,

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:22.401
and it can really sink
your teeth into something.

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:26.171
I do feel like it's evolved
into such an amazing space

00:03:26.171 --> 00:03:29.542
for actors and specifically
for young women.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:32.979
-Good. Good for you. I love that
you did this and produce this.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:35.915
-Thank you.
-It's a really fun show.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.117
I want to show everyone a clip
from next week's episode

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.586
of "Cruel Summer."
Take a look.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:41.854
-Do you think
Jamie will be here?

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.523
He can't resist the dunk tank.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.324
-Are you the one
sitting in the hot seat?

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:46.792
-That's not funny.
-Yeah, you're right.

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:49.595
It's not. I went postal on that
girl-punching loser for you,

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:51.097
so why are you chasing him?
-I'm not.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.032
It was just a question. Relax.
-Yeah.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.533
You know Dad will murder
Jamie and you

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:55.968
if you even glance
in his direction, right?

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.271
-Dad's not here.
-Yeah, well, I am.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.105
And last I checked,
Jamie is still with Kate,

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:01.640
so even if he is here,
won't she still be with him?

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.009
-That's kind of the idea.

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:05.411
-Jeannie, I swear.
-Look, I know what I'm doing.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.546
-Yeah. Stalking Kate Wallis
is what you're --

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:10.316
-Shh!
-Whoa! "Shh!"

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:13.386
Jessica Biel, Chiara Aurelia!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.755
"Cruel Summer" airs Tuesdays

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:19.592
at 10:00 p.m. on Freeform
and on Hulu the next day.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.227
So good to see you guys.
Thanks again for being here.

